Pausing, restarting, and frames
def on_key_down(key):
    if key == keys.SPACE:
        fox.sprite = hurt  # replays if it has already finished
    if key == keys.P:
        if fox.animation_paused:  # True while paused
            fox.resume_animation()  # carry on from the same frame
        else:
            fox.pause_animation()  # freeze on the current frame
    if key == keys.R:
        fox.reset_animation()  # play again from the first frame
screen.draw.text(f"frame {fox.frame}", (10, 10))  # frame number, from 0
Setting fox.frame jumps to that frame. While the whole game is paused with game.pause(), every Actor holds its frame.

Scrolling: level.x, level.y
For a map bigger than the screen, keep the player in the middle and move the map instead. Every tile moves with level.x and level.y, and collisions, pos_to_map() and map_to_pos() keep working.
def update():
    old_x, old_y = level.x, level.y
    if keyboard.left:
        level.x += 3  # move the map right, so the rabbit seems to walk left
    if keyboard.right:
        level.x -= 3
    if keyboard.up:
        level.y += 3
    if keyboard.down:
        level.y -= 3
    if rabbit.collidelist(walls) != -1:
        level.x, level.y = old_x, old_y  # hit a wall: put the map back

